        {
          "id": "1e5e3cfd-a152-3d07-9418-ee9ff4c665fe",
          "content": {
            "id": "1e5e3cfd-a152-3d07-9418-ee9ff4c665fe",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "What the Buffett Indicator says about the bull market, AI trade",
            "description": "<p>After 60 years at the top of one of the world's biggest investment firms, Berkshire Hathaway (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-A\">BRK-A</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BRK-B\">BRK-B</a>) CEO Warren Buffett will be handing off the leadership reins to Greg Abel at the end of 2025. The Oracle of Omaha was also noted to have <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/buffett-indicator-inflation-warren-buffetts-152224321.html\">invented the Buffett Indicator,</a> which assesses the valuation of the stock market by dividing the total value of US stocks with the total US GDP (gross domestic product).</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance senior reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/brooke-dipalma/\">Brooke DiPalma</a> weighs in on how much longer the Buffett Indicator may be calling for a continued bull market, while Miramar Capital Co-Founder and senior portfolio manager Max Wasserman comments on his outlook on the AI trade when factoring in Warren Buffett's market formula.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/opening-bid/\">Opening Bid</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "After 60 years at the top of one of the world's biggest investment firms, Berkshire Hathaway (BRK-A, BRK-B) CEO Warren Buffett will be handing off the leadership reins to Greg Abel at the end of 2025. The Oracle of Omaha was also noted to have invented the Buffett Indicator, which assesses the valuation of the stock market by dividing the total value of US stocks with the total US GDP (gross domestic product). Yahoo Finance senior reporter Brooke DiPalma weighs in on how much longer the Buffett Indicator may be calling for a continued bull market, while Miramar Capital Co-Founder and senior portfolio manager Max Wasserman comments on his outlook on the AI trade when factoring in Warren Buffett's market formula. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more&nbsp;Opening Bid.",
